 little activity. In very severe COPD, complications like respirator...\n\n[Doc ID: MEDQUAD-01397#chunk-0] (relevance: 0.016)\n  Title: What to do for Hypoglycemia ?\n  Content: Question: What to do for Hypoglycemia ?\nAnswer: Diabetes-related Hypoglycemia-When people with diabetes think their blood glucose level is low, they should check it and treat the problem right away.-To treat hypoglycemia, people should have a serving of a quick-fix food, wait 15 minutes, and check their blood glucose again. They should repeat the treatment until their blood glucose is 70 mg/dL or above.-People at risk for hypoglycemia should keep quick-fix foods in the car, at workanywhere they ...\n\n[Doc ID: MEDQUAD-03543#chunk-2] (relevance: 0.016)\n  Title: What are the symptoms of COPD ?\n  Content: The test results also may help find out whether another condition, such as asthma or heart failure, is causing your symptoms. Determining COPD Severity Based on this test, your doctor can determine if you have COPD and how severe it is. There are four levels of severity for COPD:-people at risk for COPD-people with mild COPD-people with moderate COPD-people with se ..."}
